♪ I close my eyes... ♪

44
00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.799
Did you get anything
from Norman's phone?

45
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.559
No. it's been wiped remotely. But
there'll probably be some residue.

46
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.919
Paddy. this one's urgent.

47
00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.960
What did you get from his bag?
Might wanna take a look at this.

48
00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:51.480
Now you're gonna love this.
Bianca. It's er... very clever.

49
00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.199
This operation has been a total and
utter shambles from start to finish.

50
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.279
We have Emma Stoke.
completely innocent.

51
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.519
whose death went unreported
for more than 36 hours.

52
00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.799
And we have two top
Special Forces operatives

53
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.799
killed in a botched snatch.

54
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:24.439
All of it based on nothing more than
a hunch you had about Norman Stoke.

55
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.800
You. and this operation.
need to be shut down now!

56
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.119
I can't see a reason to keep
it alive. Thank you. Bianca.

57
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:38.479
I retrieved this... bag

58
00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.519
from the suspect's location.

59
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.719
So you found a bag that looks
like a million other bags.

60
00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.679
one of which the assassin
happened to have.

61
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.360
What does that prove?

62
00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.480
I took this with me through
Customs this morning.

63
00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.359
I had no idea I was bringing
a sniper rifle with me

64
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.879
and neither did Security.

65
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.200
It's a prototype. That is
actually bloody clever.

66
00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.039
The sniper took the weapon he
used to kill Fest with him.

67
00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.559
And this is how he did it.

68
00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.480
All thanks to Norman Stoke.

69
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.520
Isabel? No...

70
00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.759
It's complicated.

71
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.760
We just lost two men on an op
that supposedly no-one knew about.

72
00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.439
Let's get to the bottom of
what went wrong in Belarus

73
00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.480
as quickly as possible.

74
00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.079
In the meantime...

75
00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.440
your operation is very
much alive. Bianca.

76
00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.840
Thank you.

77
00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.359
'This is Alison.
leave a message.'

78
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.879
Hi. Alison. it's Nadine.

79
00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.679
I... I can't
tell you how sorry I am.

80
00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.200
What you must be going
through right now is just...

81
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.159
Look. I know I'm the last person
you wanna speak to right now.

82
00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.839
But I've been doing some digging
and it would mean a lot to me

83
00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.879
if you'd allow me to sit
down with you face-to-face.

84
00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.319
so I can explain what happened

85
00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:58.120
and... try and make some
sense of all of this.

86
00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.080
You deserve that.

87
00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.240
Again. I'm... so sorry.

88
00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:11.640
OK. er... call me back
when you get this. Thanks.

89
00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.080
That was very good.

90
00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.359
Well. I'm off to Hereford. see
if they've got any names for us.

91
00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.760
Why hasn't that been
done already?

92
00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.800
Oh!

93
00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:32.880
Nein.

94
00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.560
Ja. ja. ja. ja. ja. ja.

95
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.119
Naturlich.

96
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.120
Mm-hm.

97
00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.719
Hey.

98
00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.719
'Hey! Sorry I haven't called.'

99
00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.559
I knew the deal was
gonna be complicated.

100
00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.679
but it's got ridiculous.

101
00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.560
'Is everything alright?'

102
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.520
Nuria?

103
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:08.439
The other day when I
left you at the airport.

104
00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:11.360
'Yeah?'

105
00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.520
I was at Plaza Las Flores...

106
00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.240
I saw you pass in a taxi.

107
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.479
Wait. what do you mean?

108
00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.520
'I saw you in a taxi. Charles.'

109
00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.160
OK. well. I don't know who you
saw but it definitely wasn't me.

110
00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.239
But I saw you.

111
00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.399
Nuria. I have no idea who you saw.
but I was straight on that plane.

112
00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.120
I don't know where you went.

113
00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.839
Where are you now?

114
00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.079
Now. I'm in an incredibly
overpriced hotel in Amsterdam.

115
00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.919
OK. let me see.

116
00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.719
Go on video. Oh. no. please.

117
00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.559
You know I hate the
video thing. come on.

118
00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.839
Do you have a woman
with you? "

119
00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.839
Of course I don't
have a woman with me.

120
00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.640
'Then let me see you.'

121
00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:11.920
'Nuria.'

122
00:15:11.921 --> 00:15:14.679
Charles. let me see you or I
will come to Amsterdam tonight.

123
00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.720
OK. OK. Alright. alright.

124
00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:26.600
Hello. it's your husband.
Look. wait. wait. wait.

125
00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.680
No woman.

126
00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:33.480
Let me see the
bathroom. Honestly?

127
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.320
OK. let's do this.

128
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.000
So... There's um...

129
00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:49.639
no make-up. no creams. no jars.

130
00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.719
No woman.

131
00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.800
'Satisfied?'

132
00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.919
She might be a very ugly woman.

133
00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:00.719
Yeah. I only have
affairs with incredibly ugly women.

134
00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.320
Now can I see my son. please?

135
00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.600
'Ma?'

136
00:16:08.601 --> 00:16:11.679
Ma? Que vea Carlitos.

137
00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.679
Mira. mira. mira! Hola.

138
00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.039
Oh!

139
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.759
Oh! Que?

140
00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.199
Hi.

141
00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.399
Que tal?

142
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:25.039
Look at him. I think. I
think his face has changed.

143
00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.479
Is that possible?

144
00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.079
Hola! A-bo!

145
00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:30.879
- A-bo!
- I miss him. Adios a papa.

146
00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.159
Bye-bye.
I love you. Bye-bye.

147
00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.560
I miss him.

148
00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.680
'He misses you.'

149
00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:49.280
I'm coming to Amsterdam.

150
00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.959
I would love that.

151
00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:56.879
but I think they've probably
got me leaving tomorrow. so...

152
00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:00.239
What's wrong. Charles?
You don't want me to come?

153
00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.559
No. I would love you to come.
but I... at the moment. honestly.

154
00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:07.559
Nuria. it's so frenzied here that
I literally don't have a minute.

155
00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.439
This life we're living.
it's not normal.

156
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.799
Yeah. I know it's not.

157
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:16.319
'You're always away.
For business you say.

158
00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.079
but you never tell me
anything about your business.

159
00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.199
I never met any of
your colleagues.'

160
00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.799
I don't know what you
do when you're away.

161
00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:26.319
'I work. Nuria.

162
00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:30.000
I work. that's all
I do. I just work.'

163
00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.519
When are you coming back?

164
00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.919
Soon. a couple of days. I-

165
00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.119
'When?' I... Honestly.
I don't know.

166
00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.440
I'm not sure.

167
00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:42.720
You never know.

168
00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.759
It's not good enough. Charles.

169
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.320
Are you coming?

170
00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:30.840
Love. are you coming?

171
00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.520
They get you over here
to identify her...

172
00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:39.840
and then they don't
even fucking call you.

173
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.080
Bit of fresh air
will do you good.

174
00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:50.719
You go.

175
00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.880
Who's this? 'Who the
fuck do you think it is?'

176
00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.800
About ye. Norman?

177
00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:53.119
I'm so sorry about Emma.

178
00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.959
I can't imagine what
you're going through.

179
00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:58.199
No. you can't.

180
00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:01.359
Larry and me are here
to take Emma home.

181
00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.119
Can you not just let us do that?

182
00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.960
Do you have no common decency?

183
00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:15.119
You said on the phone
you'd been digging?

184
00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:16.959
I've spoken to everybody.

185
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:20.840
And I have to tell you that
no one behaved improperly.

186
00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:26.840
Did you know that Emma had - a pre-existing condition?
- No.

187
00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.759
First I heard of it was when
they rang us to tell us the news.

188
00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:34.079
It could just as easily have
happened at home. in bed.

189
00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:36.239
But she wasn't in
her bed. was she?

190
00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:38.639
She was in a police cell
and you put her there.

191
00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:40.559
I didn't. Alison. And
I've told you that.

192
00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:43.360
Do you even know
what the truth is?

193
00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:46.559
Listen to me carefully. Alison.

194
00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:52.440
Norman killed two British officers
yesterday and now he's disappeared.

195
00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:56.239
What's that got to do with me?
That's nothing to do with me.

196
00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.799
Larry's number was in
Norman's phone. So...

197
00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:02.479
We were trying to
get the money to go to London.

198
00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:03.720
Alison.

199
00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:08.640
Assisting an offender
carries a ten-year sentence.

200
00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:12.960
More. with everything
Larry's been up to.

201
00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:17.520
But I've turned a blind
eye because I like you...

202
00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:21.400
and I want to help.

203
00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:25.640
But now you have to help me.

204
00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:29.879
You need to tell
me where Norman is.

205
00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.520
Fuck off!

206
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.160
Did you have a nice walk?

207
00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:08.800
Larry. is everything alright?

208
00:24:27.240 --> 00:24:29.919
What have you done?

209
00:24:29.920 --> 00:24:31.960
What?

210
00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:40.200
Why did you keep on
at me to call Norman?

211
00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:44.600
We needed the money
to go to London.

212
00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:51.560
Do you know what happened to
Norman... after I called him?

213
00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:55.839
How would I?

214
00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:58.240
What happened?

215
00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:01.240
They came for him.

216
00:25:04.320 --> 00:25:06.320
He popped a couple of 'em.

217
00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:11.160
Is he all right?

218
00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:18.959
Gimme your phone.

219
00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:20.760
Larry. what are you on about?

220
00:25:21.880 --> 00:25:24.080
Give me your phone.

221
00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.880
Who's Nadine?

222
00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:51.520
She's the new girl
at the hairdresser's.

223
00:25:52.680 --> 00:25:56.240
So if I call the hairdresser's
now and ask for Nadine...

224
00:25:57.280 --> 00:25:59.560
is Nadine gonna
come on the phone?

225
00:26:00.640 --> 00:26:02.520
She might do. I don't know.

226
00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:07.399
Larry. why are you
being like this?

227
00:26:07.400 --> 00:26:09.920
Oh. Alison.

228
00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:13.040
Alison.

229
00:26:15.400 --> 00:26:17.480
What have you done?

230
00:26:19.520 --> 00:26:22.480
What the fuck have you done?

231
00:26:24.880 --> 00:26:27.319
No. don't. Larry.

232
00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:29.360
No!

233
00:26:50.960 --> 00:26:53.959
Cease fire!

234
00:26:53.960 --> 00:26:55.959
Stand up!

235
00:26:58.240 --> 00:27:00.280
Make safe!

236
00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:03.800
Thank you. gentlemen.

237
00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:11.599
These individuals all meet
the parameters I was given.

238
00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:13.799
Do you think any of these men
could have made that shot?

239
00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:16.999
Not unless they've improved
massively from when they were here.

240
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.319
Are you a hundred percent
certain about the distance?

241
00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:21.799
3.815 metres.

242
00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:24.519
That's a fucking long way. That's
what the Germans are saying.

243
00:27:24.520 --> 00:27:25.999
With all due respect
to the Germans.

244
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.439
I suggest someone
re-measures the distance.

245
00:27:28.440 --> 00:27:31.039
or else puts me in touch with
whoever modified the weapon.

246
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:34.359
because whoever it is. he
knows how to make guns.

247
00:27:34.360 --> 00:27:36.759
We could make very
good use of him here.

248
00:27:36.760 --> 00:27:39.200
Yeah. well. thanks for this.

249
00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:43.319
Norman definitely
knew we were coming.

250
00:27:43.320 --> 00:27:47.039
His bags were packed. and
he was ready for a fight.

251
00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:51.199
What's your annual salary?

252
00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:54.759
You know my grade. you
know the pay scales.

253
00:27:54.760 --> 00:27:57.639
And your husband. he's
not a professor. is he?

254
00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:02.759
He's lower down the
university pecking order?

255
00:28:02.760 --> 00:28:04.959
He's a senior lecturer.
Senior lecturer?

256
00:28:04.960 --> 00:28:08.919
So. what does Paul earn? 40. 50?

257
00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:13.120
So it's a comfortable
joint wage. but not mega.

258
00:28:14.280 --> 00:28:18.199
Is there family money?

259
00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:21.239
Your father was...
What was he? Missing.

260
00:28:21.240 --> 00:28:25.239
And your mother? Has nothing
to do with Norman Stoke.

261
00:28:25.240 --> 00:28:26.959
You've been on this
side of the table.

262
00:28:26.960 --> 00:28:29.320
You know why I'm asking.

263
00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:36.959
My mother. if that's what you
wanna call her. was an alcoholic.

264
00:28:36.960 --> 00:28:39.119
She still is.

265
00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:42.199
She lives in sheltered housing
now. Which you pay for.

266
00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:45.920
Must cost quite a penny.

267
00:28:46.880 --> 00:28:51.599
Are you suggesting
I tipped off Norman Stoke

268
00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:54.039
to pay for my mother's
sheltered housing?

269
00:28:54.040 --> 00:28:56.720
Money is almost
always the motive.

270
00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:01.639
Let me tell you something. yeah.

271
00:29:01.640 --> 00:29:05.759
I almost got killed
trying to GET Norman.

272
00:29:05.760 --> 00:29:09.319
Two of the men I
was with are dead.

273
00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:12.839
You know I didn't tip him off so
why you going through this charade?

274
00:29:12.840 --> 00:29:16.119
You know the world we live in.

275
00:29:16.120 --> 00:29:18.879
You can't trust anyone.

276
00:29:18.880 --> 00:29:21.919
Everyone lies.

277
00:29:21.920 --> 00:29:24.680
About everything.

278
00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.320
No.

279
00:30:53.880 --> 00:30:56.559
Damian? The Special
Forces gave me a list

280
00:30:56.560 --> 00:30:58.679
of the best snipers
who fit our parameters.

281
00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:01.119
but they don't think any of
them could have made that shot.

282
00:31:01.120 --> 00:31:04.279
Well. check them out anyway.
Yeah. I will. just got to...

283
00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:07.400
Yep. yeah. Yeah.

284
00:31:29.080 --> 00:31:32.479
Anything on Norman Stoke?

285
00:31:32.480 --> 00:31:35.279
Er... I spoke to
Sparrow in person.

286
00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:38.239
Did you get anything?

287
00:31:38.240 --> 00:31:43.479
Well. she's devastated
and angry about Emma.

288
00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:46.640
She's not in the mood to talk.

289
00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:51.359
When did you last get some
sleep? I'm fine. honestly.

290
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:53.359
I need you firing
on all cylinders.

291
00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:56.880
Go home. get some rest.

292
00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:14.159
'Can anyone hear us?'

293
00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:16.719
Why are you calling me
on my personal phone?

294
00:32:16.720 --> 00:32:18.439
What's going on?

295
00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:38.640
I've just had the pleasure
of Carver's company.

296
00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:42.159
How was that for you?

297
00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:44.920
Unpleasant. and I've
got nothing to hide.

298
00:32:45.840 --> 00:32:49.799
But if there's a leak. it has
to be investigated and resolved.

299
00:32:49.800 --> 00:32:53.439
Something definitely
went wrong in Belarus.

300
00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:55.760
Norman knew we were coming.

301
00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:04.959
Let's assume for present purposes.
it's not you and it's not me.

302
00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:07.479
OK.

303
00:33:07.480 --> 00:33:10.599
The only other people who
knew about the operation

304
00:33:10.600 --> 00:33:12.239
are Damian and Isabel.

305
00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:16.399
Well. if it's
Isabel. we're all fucked.

306
00:33:16.400 --> 00:33:19.279
Indeed.

307
00:33:19.280 --> 00:33:23.760
Could it be Damian?
Why would Damian do it?

308
00:33:24.960 --> 00:33:28.119
Not an easy fellow to
pin down. is he. Damian?

309
00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:30.160
Has a sort of...
slippery quality.

310
00:33:31.920 --> 00:33:34.000
Why are we here?

311
00:33:35.920 --> 00:33:37.719
Just to be on the safe side.

312
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:40.919
what I'm going to tell you
doesn't go any further.

313
00:33:40.920 --> 00:33:43.280
Agreed? Agreed.

314
00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:50.159
An American friend
has been in contact.

315
00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:53.199
Unofficial. back channel.

316
00:33:53.200 --> 00:33:55.239
I've known him for 20 years.

317
00:33:55.240 --> 00:33:57.599
Ex-station chief in
Ankara and Tokyo.

318
00:33:57.600 --> 00:34:01.479
Level-headed. very judicious.

319
00:34:01.480 --> 00:34:03.639
The Yanks are worried that
the assassination of Fest

320
00:34:03.640 --> 00:34:06.879
will spark copycat
murders of politicians.

321
00:34:06.880 --> 00:34:08.599
They're very keen to
get to the bottom of it

322
00:34:08.600 --> 00:34:11.119
and had been liaising
closely with us.

323
00:34:11.120 --> 00:34:13.319
But now his department
has been told

324
00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.640
to not share any
information with 303.

325
00:34:18.160 --> 00:34:21.479
Well. either Carver's right

326
00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:24.560
or the Americans are
trying to sabotage us.

327
00:34:25.960 --> 00:34:28.679
The Americans didn't know
about the Belarus operation

328
00:34:28.680 --> 00:34:30.920
until after it happened.

329
00:34:35.560 --> 00:34:37.320
So... if my friend is right.

330
00:34:39.200 --> 00:34:41.360
the problem is in-house.

331
00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:52.519
From here on. keep
the circle tight.

332
00:36:33.720 --> 00:36:37.159
Good morning. 'Have you
checked your account?'

333
00:36:37.160 --> 00:36:39.479
Er. I saw that the er.
commencement fee had landed. yeah.

334
00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:41.159
Good.

335
00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:44.399
Rodin is going to be
in Tallinn on the 22nd.

336
00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:46.799
If you leave now you'll have
plenty of time to prepare.

337
00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:51.239
'How reliable's that
information?' A hundred percent.

338
00:36:51.240 --> 00:36:54.079
Understood. I will start
making arrangements.

339
00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:58.279
And we're assuming you finished
whatever business you had in Munich?

340
00:36:58.280 --> 00:37:00.519
Well. that seems like
a decent assumption.

341
00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:03.159
'Good to hear. We've
paid you a lot of money

342
00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:05.119
and we expect to have
your complete attention.'

343
00:37:05.120 --> 00:37:07.240
Absolutely.

344
00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:02.239
How was the Carver experience?

345
00:38:02.240 --> 00:38:04.439
Yeah. he was just doing
his job. I suppose.

346
00:38:04.440 --> 00:38:06.319
Here's the list of snipers.

347
00:38:06.320 --> 00:38:09.639
Appallingly analogue. I know.
But that's the Army for you.

348
00:38:09.640 --> 00:38:12.719
And they've all left the Service.
Thompson's in prison. Manslaughter.

349
00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:15.519
Clegg has MS. I have
addresses for the others.

350
00:38:15.520 --> 00:38:17.839
What do you want me to do?

351
00:38:17.840 --> 00:38:22.119
Find out where they were - when Fest was killed.
- Copy that.

352
00:38:22.120 --> 00:38:24.079
Thank you. Anything
from Sparrow?

353
00:38:24.080 --> 00:38:26.959
Not yet. Bianca.

354
00:38:26.960 --> 00:38:29.640
Found something very
interesting on the phone.

355
00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:34.319
Can you get me a coffee. please?

356
00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:37.680
Er. black. no sugar.

357
00:38:42.160 --> 00:38:43.519
Cheers.

358
00:38:43.520 --> 00:38:46.679
Eh. what you got for
me? Well. it was tough.

359
00:38:46.680 --> 00:38:49.879
There's some very serious
encryptions. I'd say state level.

360
00:38:49.880 --> 00:38:52.199
Almost all of the data's
been wiped remotely.

361
00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:54.799
And we were only able to recover
incoming and outgoing numbers.

362
00:38:54.800 --> 00:38:57.039
None of the content but...

363
00:38:57.040 --> 00:38:59.319
in the three weeks leading
up to Manfred Fest's murder.

364
00:38:59.320 --> 00:39:02.279
there was a flurry of calls and
messages from a single number.

365
00:39:02.280 --> 00:39:04.039
Now. interestingly.

366
00:39:04.040 --> 00:39:06.519
they stopped completely
the day Fest was murdered.

367
00:39:06.520 --> 00:39:10.639
Did you get a name for the
caller? Yeah. well. Jackal.

368
00:39:10.640 --> 00:39:12.959
Jackal? Well. it's
codename. obviously.

369
00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:14.639
Alright.

370
00:39:14.640 --> 00:39:18.320
Alright. I'll leave
you to it. Cheers.

371
00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:51.279
Frau Muller. Herr Fest.

372
00:43:04.961 --> 00:43:07.079
Muller!

373
00:43:07.080 --> 00:43:08.640
Muller!

374
00:43:09.640 --> 00:43:12.839
Muller! Muller!

375
00:44:22.800 --> 00:44:24.640
No...

376
00:44:25.640 --> 00:44:27.639
You know who I am.

377
00:44:27.640 --> 00:44:32.040
Look. I'm... I'm sorry.

378
00:44:33.920 --> 00:44:36.239
I... I hired you to shoot my
father and then you shot me.

379
00:44:36.240 --> 00:44:38.439
So I was just... I was mad.

380
00:44:38.440 --> 00:44:41.520
Ah. ah. I was just mad.

381
00:44:42.680 --> 00:44:44.839
See it from my point
of view. please.

382
00:44:44.840 --> 00:44:46.599
Huh?

383
00:44:46.600 --> 00:44:49.559
I'll pay you. I
promise. I promise.

384
00:44:49.560 --> 00:44:53.800
I'll pay you... I'll pay
you whatever you want.

385
00:45:00.640 --> 00:45:02.599
But it's not about the money.

386
00:45:09.800 --> 00:45:12.199
Elias.

387
00:45:14.560 --> 00:45:16.600
Elias.

388
00:45:24.440 --> 00:45:27.199
Fuck... You.

389
00:45:39.760 --> 00:45:41.840
Won't Get Fooled Again

